===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{1|first-rate}}; of the highest quality; exceptionally good.
#: {{ux|en|This champagne is '''superb'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I|text=Captain Edward Carlisle{{...}}felt a curious sensation of helplessness seize upon him as he met her steady gaze,{{nb...}}; he could not tell what this prisoner might do. He cursed the fate which had assigned such a duty, cursed especially that fate which forced a gallant soldier to meet so '''superb''' a woman as this under handicap so hard.}}
# Grand; magnificent; august; stately.
#: {{ux|en|a '''superb''' edifice;&emsp; a '''superb''' colonnade}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} {{1|haughty}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1858|author=w:Julia Kavanagh|title=Adèle, a Tale: Volume 2|page=235
|passage=A remark which Isabella received with a '''superb''' curl of the lip, but at the same time, and to her brother's infinite relief, she walked away.}}

